# People

- `src/people.js` owns the cast, atlas keys, raster choice and biome traveller
  row. Add a person through the body table. Keep one cast list.
- `src/body-folk.js` owns integer anatomy, contact and garment landmarks. Human
  joints stay grid-authored.
- `src/figure-folk.js` owns raster concessions and garment drawing.
- `src/culture.js` owns dress, fashion vocabulary, weather selection and ramps.
  Body modules carry no appearance choices.

Closest check: `npm run test:folk:contract` for anatomy, states, views and gait,
`test:folk:raster` for connectedness, stems, face and cues, `test:folk:colour`
for ramps, hierarchy and dress, `test:culture` for vocabulary, `test:people` for
the cluster. `node tools/person.mjs <name>` draws one person.

`src/gear.js` owns wearable items: a named fold over a fashion row, refused by
weather, palette or slot. `tools/lineup.mjs <biome>` draws the roster at one
scale; `npm run test:cast` holds silhouette distance, `test:gear` the items.
The `add-character` skill carries the row order.
